    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor. His score of 78.66 is driven by an elite .443 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Jack Perkins. While we await official confirmation, his assumed #2 spot in the order provides a high-leverage opportunity to maximize run production. Behind him, **Junior Caminero** (68.59) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.84) are our next tier of high-impact starters; **Nootbaar** specifically benefits from an 11% platoon bump against Buehler, positioning him as an essential contributor in the leadoff spot despite a slightly negative park factor. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Josh Smith** (64.65) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (63.68) against Lowder, where the pitcher\u2019s high xERA of 4.84 and his notoriously slow delivery create a massive ceiling for our baserunners to exploit.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Dillon Dingler** being the only consideration who threatened the starting lineup. Ultimately, **Dillon Dingler** posted a 36.38 score, falling below our mandatory 40-point floor for activation. While his ability to face a pitcher with a slow delivery theoretically aids our stolen base pursuit, a significant -14% penalty due to the opponent's pitching skill and a poor platoon split against Yates rendered him too risky to deploy. Elsewhere, we are navigating rest days for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Caleb Durbin**, ensuring our roster management preserves games for the season's closing stretch. While **Carson Benge** sits at a marginal 45.61 due to a difficult L/L platoon matchup, he maintains his spot in the lineup, as we lack superior bench alternatives to pivot toward tonight.",
